  "body": "Some homes are simply built to sell. This spacious four-bedroom residence was built to live in - and it shows.\r\n\r\nConstructed by a respected local builder during Millwater's early development, 5 Portland Park Road was chosen by its current owners for its considered layout, high specification, and quality of finish - and it has been maintained to a standard that genuinely presents as better than new.\r\n\r\nStep through solid timber flooring into a light-filled entrance and reception room, where impressive stud heights, plentiful Venetian-dressed windows, and detailed timber skirting and cornicing immediately set the tone. A partially open dining room links through to the heart of the home: a light, bright open-plan kitchen and living area, beneath a feature vaulted ceiling, which opens via bi-fold doors onto a private, beautifully landscaped garden. \r\n\r\nThe kitchen itself is thoughtfully laid out with generous storage, solid timber flooring, and a substantial stone benchtop with waterfall edge.\r\n\r\nTwo good-sized bedrooms with built-in wardrobes sit on the ground floor, served by a family bathroom and separate WC — ideal for children, visiting parents, or a self-contained guest wing. \r\nUpstairs, a substantial master suite offers a fully tiled bathroom with a second bathtub and a walk-in robe. \r\nAn additional bedroom or guest room, sits alongside a separate study nook. \r\n\r\nA carpeted, internal-access double garage houses the laundry, with side access to the washing line and a garden shed.\r\n\r\nSet on a premium residential street, this home is an easy walk to Millwater's shops, cafés, and\r\nreputable local schools, with Orewa's beaches, the wider Hibiscus Coast, and Silverdale's growing retail and dining scene all just minutes away. For commuters, the rapid bus network links Millwater straight through to Albany and onward to central Auckland — lifestyle and connectivity, without compromise.\r\n\r\nWhether you're upsizing for a growing family, downsizing without giving up quality and space, planning ahead for the net stage of life, relocating home from overseas, or looking for a layout that comfortably suits multiple generations under one roof - this home has been designed, built, and cared for to make that transition easy. \r\n\r\nCommitted to selling, the vendors have made their decision - now it's your turn. This is a genuine opportunity to secure a home of this calibre on one of Millwater's premium streets, with a clear and transparent path to ownership.\r\n\r\nFor more information or to arrange a private viewing - Please get in touch",
